Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||04-14-2001||08:23 AM||||One reason for this that I know of is that when you adjust your valve lash, each mark represents the proper position to adjust the valves. Refrence that in your manuals and you'll see what I mean.<BR>When adjusting the engine timing you use the widest mark, as this represents #1 and #4 cylinder TDC.||||reg||1
